<title>CROATIA: Croatian Feb currency reserves rise to $4.2 bln.</title>
<headline>Croatian Feb currency reserves rise to $4.2 bln.</headline>
<dateline>ZAGREB 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Croatia issued the following economic indicator details.</p>
<p> CROATIA CURRENCY RESERVES  FEBRUARY    JANUARY	FEB '96</p>
<p> Total (million USD)	  4,191.8     4,086.9	3,424.4</p>
<p> National Bank of Croatia   2,177.8     2,173.1	1,883.6</p>
<p> Commercial banks	     2,014.0     1,913.8	1,540.8</p>
<p>NOTE -- The central bank's international reserves rose 0.2 percent on a monthly basis after shrinking 6.1 percent due to stronger dollar in January. Commercial banks' February reserves rose 5.2 percent after a 3.9-percent dip a month earlier. -- Zagreb Newsroom, 385-1-4557075</p>
</text>
